ers/enigmaticrex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"89c474a61cfc675fe91f625e5b0ba246a669b1cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commits/89c474a61cfc675fe91f625e5b0ba246a669b1cc","html_url":"https://github.com/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commit/89c474a61cfc675fe91f625e5b0ba246a669b1cc"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"8c9042ab8171e9afb9e4d790413d7b32058746f6","node_id":"C_kwDOTzGnatoAKDhjOTA0MmFiODE3MWU5YWZiOWU0ZDc5MDQxM2Q3YjMyMDU4NzQ2ZjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"sain.saji","email":"sain.sajix@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-03T15:56:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"sain.saji","email":"sain.sajix@gmail.com","date":"2026-09-03T15:56:26Z"},"message":"#57: fall back to FFmpeg when the native decoder goes fatal\n\nRoot cause: #31 (efa80fb) routed 4K H.264 to the resident sceVideodec2\ndecoder. For most streams that's fine and seek works (GTA 4K, 1080p,\n720p all verified). But some streams - Tears of Steel 3840x1714 is the\nknown one - fail sceVideodec2Decode with 0x811d0303 on the first AU after\na mid-stream sceVideodec2Reset (seek). The one fixed-size resident decoder\n(created pre-unjail, can't be re-sized per file) doesn't cleanly re-accept\nthat stream after a reset. Before #31 these played on FFmpeg, which seeks\nreliably - hence \"worked till yesterday\".\n\nWhen the native backend hits the fatal streak, instead of ending the\nsession: set a sticky per-file g_vdec_force_ffmpeg, reopen the file on\nFFmpeg at the current position, toast \"Switched to software decode\".\nFFmpeg then handles that file (and its seeks) for the rest of the session.\nA genuinely undecodable file still ends cleanly (the flag is already set,\nso no reopen loop). A different file re-enables native.\n\n- g_vdec_force_ffmpeg + per-path reset in start_video_playback\n- vp.backend gate\n- evo_pb_reset_decode_fatal() clears the streak too (not just the flag),\n  so the FFmpeg reopen isn't instantly re-tripped\n- 016_VDEC_FFMPEG_FALLBACK breadcrumb\n\nThe bsf-rebuild-on-seek from 5b4065c stays (correct regardless; wasn't the\nTears cause). Proper native-decode-reset robustness is separate (#38/#39).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea9932d2977eeba53a21221aa0becc4b93bdf65d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/git/trees/ea9932d2977eeba53a21221aa0becc4b93bdf65d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/git/commits/8c9042ab8171e9afb9e4d790413d7b32058746f6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commits/8c9042ab8171e9afb9e4d790413d7b32058746f6","html_url":"https://github.com/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commit/8c9042ab8171e9afb9e4d790413d7b32058746f6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sainsaji/EVO-PLAYER-PS5/commits/8c9042ab8171e9afb9e4d790413d7b32058746f6/comments","author":{"login":"enigmaticrex","id":56771208,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NzcxMjA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56771208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex","html_url":"https://github.com/enigmaticrex","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enigmaticrex/received_even